---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Traditional Wear Itineraries: 5, 7 & 14 Day Trips"
  description="Three detailed itineraries: 5-day Xi'an Hanfu deep dive, 7-day Beijing-Xi'an triangle, 14-day Silk Road of Style across five cities. Plan your trip."
  canonicalUrl="/plan-trip/itineraries"
  articleDate="2026-08-03"
  breadcrumbs={{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Plan Your Trip", url: "/plan-trip/" }, { name: "Itineraries", url: "/plan-trip/itineraries/" }}>
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#b5343a] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase">Plan Your Trip · Itineraries</span>
    <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">Sample Itineraries: 5, 7 & 14 Days</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">Each itinerary built around traditional clothing experiences, combining costume activities with essential sightseeing.</p>
    <div class="mt-12 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-6"><span class="text-xs px-2.5 py-1 bg-stone-500 text-white rounded-full font-medium">5 Days</span><h2 class="font-serif-sc text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-3">Xi''an Hanfu Deep Dive</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-2">One city, maximum immersion. Day 1: arrive, Muslim Quarter. Day 2: Hanfu rental + city wall photoshoot all day. Day 3: Terracotta Warriors + Shaanxi Museum. Day 4: second Hanfu day with different dynasty style, Daming Palace + Datang Everbright City. Day 5: shopping + departure.</p><p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-3">Cost: 3,200-5,500 RMB | Best: April-May or Sept-Oct</p></div>
    <div class="mt-8 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-6"><span class="text-xs px-2.5 py-1 bg-[#b5343a] text-white rounded-full font-medium">7 Days</span><h2 class="font-serif-sc text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-3">Beijing to Xi''an: Tang Suit + Hanfu</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-2">Days 1-2: Beijing tang suit fitting, Forbidden City photos at Jingshan Park. Day 3: Great Wall + train to Xi''an. Days 4-6: Full Hanfu experience in Xi''an. Day 7: departure.</p><p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-3">Cost: 4,800-10,100 RMB | Train Beijing to Xi''an: 515 RMB</p></div>
    <div class="mt-8 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-6"><span class="text-xs px-2.5 py-1 bg-[#b5343a] text-white rounded-full font-medium">14 Days</span><h2 class="font-serif-sc text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-3">Silk Road of Style: 5 Cities</h2><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-2">Shanghai (custom qipao + vintage shopping) to Suzhou (silk qipao garden photoshoot) to Hangzhou (Song hanfu + silk museum) to Nanjing (Ming hanfu) to Xi''an (Tang + Ming Hanfu). The full fashion journey.</p><p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-3">Cost: 9,000-18,000 RMB | 5 train rides: ~1,000-1,500 RMB</p></div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">How to Customize These Itineraries</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">These routes are optimized for traditional clothing experiences, but they work as a strong backbone. Add 1-2 extra days in each city if you want to go deeper into sightseeing — most first-timers underestimate how much time Hanfu and qipao activities take (plan minimum 4-5 hours for a full rental + photoshoot day). For photographers who want serious shots: book your Hanfu experience for early morning (8-10 AM) when sites are least crowded, or late afternoon (3-5 PM) for golden hour light. Avoid Chinese national holidays — especially the first week of October and Spring Festival — when every site is packed and prices double.</p>
    <div class="mt-8"><a href="/plan-trip" class="text-sm text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors">Back to Plan Your Trip</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
